WEBVTT

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:05.770
It's so gooey and stretchy!

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:07.940
This is great!

00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:01.600
Spring is still so
far away.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.140
Phew, the thesis presentation's over at last.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.730
It feels like we're finally done with college.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:12.480
I've gotta go to school starting next week.

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.480
Really? Before the semester starts?

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.650
Teaching at a girls' high school sounds rough.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.200
U-Um...

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.070
Hey, why don't we go get tea or something?

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:22.700
Sounds great.

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.950
You coming, Uchiki?

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.250
I, uh...

00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:31.080
My ears are itching, so I'll have to pass!

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:39.220
She's kinda strange, isn't she?

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:54.020
<i>I feel like spring's never, ever going to come.</i>

00:02:55.780 --> 00:03:00.030
<i>On days like this, I have my favorite.</i>

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:13.840
Lots of people skipped class today.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.340
Same here.

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:21.760
Exams are coming up soon, so I'd imagine they'd rather stay home and study.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:23.430
I suppose.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:25.560
It does feel like it's almost time for the main event.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:29.560
The main event...

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.310
Those are the uniforms of the school we want to go to.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:38.570
They look so cute.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.820
What's wrong, Morino?

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:46.200
I just feel really nervous all of a sudden.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.200
Really?

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.910
About whether I'll get in.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.170
About whether I'll make any friends there if I do.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.170
We'll see about the first part, but I know you'll be fine on the second.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.380
You're so upbeat. You'll make friends in no time.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:06.010
But I don't have any friends from here other than you guys,

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.310
and I've been coming here for over a year.

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:12.100
You always come and go with us.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.350
All we do at cram school is draw, anyway.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.360
I guess, but...

00:04:17.980 --> 00:04:21.610
You really are nervous today.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.860
It's that time of year.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:32.500
You're staying overnight, right?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:33.160
Yeah.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:35.420
Let's rent a movie, then.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.420
A little fun will take our minds off things.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.170
This is taking our minds off things?!

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:43.840
Brrrraaaaaaaaaiiiiiinnnnnnsssss...

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:48.470
Y-You call this fun?!

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:53.390
Yep. It's best to let out your stress with a good scream.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:56.150
I don't think this is what I need!

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.020
Frrrrriiieeeeeeennndddsss...

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.900
Frrrrrrriiiiiieeeeeeennnnnddddssss....

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.900
I think I get where it's coming from.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:09.160
You're sympathizing with a horror movie?!

00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:14.750
Now I'm <i>really</i> worried about everything.

00:05:14.750 --> 00:05:16.830
Everything? Like what?

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:22.590
Well, exams and friends, like I said, but there's something else too.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.260
It's supposed to snow next week, right?

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.970
If it snows too much, what happens to our fields?

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:34.730
If we keep ruining the environment,
how many more years can the Earth last?

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:38.350
The Earth itself? That's a pretty big problem to worry about.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:41.400
Aren't you worried about anything, Ryo?

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.480
Me?

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:47.410
Exams, of course, but...

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.160
Isn't there anything else at all?
Even something little?

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:57.960
I am a little bit nervous about the snow. I guess you could say I'm worried.

00:05:57.960 --> 00:06:00.710
I wonder if I should do the laundry inside or...

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:06.720
I forgot! I put the futons out to air earlier!

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.930
Oh no!

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:13.100
They're all cold.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:16.810
But they're still dry, so they'll be fine.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:18.230
No way.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:21.650
I'm never going to make any friends.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.650
That's not true.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.110
You might be shy, but you're still kind and honest.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.400
You just need to keep trying.

00:06:28.820 --> 00:06:31.410
No, it just won't work.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:35.040
You're always so outgoing. You'd never understand.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.660
It sounds like she's talking to someone.

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:41.080
I guess she has her window open?

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.540
I just want to come back home.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:46.170
How's Dad? How about Spot?

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:49.720
I think she's on the phone.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.300
Kirin...

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.140
I can't do this anymore.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:58.310
What do you mean, just be friendly?

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:02.900
Why don't we just pretend we didn't hear this?

00:07:03.770 --> 00:07:05.360
Belly dancing?!

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:09.200
Normal girls don't do that!

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:11.740
This is pretty embarrassing.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:17.240
I'm so terrified of whether I'll be able to fit in that I feel like I'm going to die.

00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:24.420
See? She's just like me.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:30.510
We shouldn't keep eavesdropping.
Let's go back inside.

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.510
Kirin!

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:53.860
This is Uchiki Yuki. She lives here.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:57.370
Pleased to meet you.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:08:02.750
And this is my cousin. She stays over every weekend.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.580
I'm Morino Kirin.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:08.630
Kirin, don't you have something to say to Ms. Uchiki?

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:15.390
I'm sorry. I tried to catch a falling sheet and fell right along with it.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:19.390
I ended up needing to borrow your veranda to save myself.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.900
<i>Her reflexes are amazing!</i>

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:29.570
We're really sorry for scaring you like that.

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:33.900
Oh, don't worry about it.
It's partly my fault too.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:39.410
<i>I had no idea I'd left the window open while I was on the phone.</i>

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:45.670
<i>I can't believe I let them hear something so embarrassing.</i>

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:50.550
<i>That's the only reason why she fell from the second floor and they're here apologizing to me now.</i>

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:57.550
<i>I'm so embarrassed I just want to crawl into a hole in the ground.</i>

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.770
We're really sorry!

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:06.020
<i>We need to leave before we make her feel any worse.</i>

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.310
Anyway, Kirin...

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:11.280
You know, I'm worried too!

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.990
Worried about getting into a high school.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:16.450
Worried about making friends.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:19.700
I'm really worried, so I totally understand how you feel!

00:09:23.450 --> 00:09:26.460
<i>She's so forceful about it.</i>

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:30.420
<i>She seems like a good girl.
Energetic, with a sparkle in her eyes.</i>

00:09:30.420 --> 00:09:36.470
<i>I know she'll be able to handle the pressure and make it into the school she wants to.</i>

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:42.060
<i>She's so outgoing that I know she'll have a hard time containing herself.</i>

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:44.680
<i>Maybe they'll have a graduation party to celebrate their both getting in.</i>

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:47.140
<i>That sounds great. I'm so happy for them.</i>

00:09:47.650 --> 00:09:48.520
Um...

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:52.070
I'm so happy for you!

00:09:52.070 --> 00:09:53.860
Huh? What for?

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:59.280
Oh, sorry! I was overthinking things and—

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:02.790
I just have a hard time saying what I think.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:07.330
I get so nervous around people I don't know.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.540
I'm really bad at expressing myself.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:20.550
It's been years since I've been able to say what I want to.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:28.230
So I've only ever made two friends.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.230
Two?

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:31.770
Why not get in touch with them?

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:35.190
They don't carry transceivers or anything, so...

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:39.570
I wonder how you're doing, Tweety? Fluffy?

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:46.620
Are those names...

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:50.170
It's been cold this winter, so I'm worried about them.

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:54.800
Don't worry. I'm sure they'll be there when you go back home.

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:57.300
Yeah, I just know they're fine!

00:10:58.380 --> 00:11:01.890
<i>These two are being so kind to me.</i>

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.890
<i>They really are good girls.</i>

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:08.520
<i>I wish I could do something for them too.</i>

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:14.650
I'm jealous of how good you are at saying just how you feel, Kirin.

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:18.570
I know you'll be able to make friends with that kind of confidence.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:24.410
<i>...is what I wish I could say to cheer her up, but...</i>

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:29.000
<i>N-Now she's staring at me!</i>

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:40.510
Hurry Hurry Pizza!

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:42.590
Thanks.

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:46.350
Delivery pizza? Did she order it for us?!

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:50.640
It doesn't seem like she did.

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:52.900
Order again soon!

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:03.990
Do you order pizza often?

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.410
Well, uh...

00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.250
I bit my tongue...

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:21.050
Oh, each quarter has different toppings?

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.470
And you normally eat this all yourself?

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:25.010
It's more convenient this way.

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:26.760
Convenient?

00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:30.390
If I split it into, say, seafood, gratin,

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.060
barbecue,

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.810
and salami and mushroom,

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:44.110
I can have it in the morning, evening,
and suppertime, and never get sick of it.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:48.200
<i>She's right, but that's still kind of sad.</i>

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:52.370
Pizza's great. We should order one too.

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:56.830
Why don't I give you this one as thanks?

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.840
You don't need to thank us.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:04.130
All we've done is bother you,

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:06.550
so we couldn't accept something that expensive.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:11.390
No, no. I've burdened you with my problems,

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.520
and I can just order another one.

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:22.780
If it's okay with you, how about we all share it in my apartment?

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.870
Th-Thanks.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:29.280
Come right in!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.830
It's laid out a little bit differently.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:44.550
<i>This apartment is wonderful. It's so much airier than mine!</i>

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:47.430
She's gone quiet again.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:52.060
<i>We're in the same building,
so why does it feel so different?</i>

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:56.310
<i>The interior's not quite the same, but...</i>

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:58.900
<i>I think what it really is</i>

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:04.070
<i>is that I made mine so gloomy.</i>

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.570
She's thinking about something again!

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:11.080
I don't know what you're worried about, but I'm sure it's a misunderstanding!

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.200
Then...

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.040
Let's eat!

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:32.680
Soft, chewy cheese wrapping around the fresh seafood sauce...

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.720
Its tastiness extends to the horizon!

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:38.560
If it were a sea, I'd want to dive right in!

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:44.070
The cheese in the crust makes it feel like I'm eating a fancy kind of bread.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:47.070
And then the normal salami and mushroom...

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:51.570
It's so safe and steady that I just want to move in right on top of it!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:08.920
<i>Wow, they seem like they're enjoying themselves so much.</i>

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:11.640
<i>It's incredible.</i>

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:15.560
<i>Being watched while I eat is a bit...</i>

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:17.430
<i>Embarrassing...</i>

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:20.270
Aren't you going to have any, Uchiki?

00:15:20.270 --> 00:15:22.980
No, go ahead. You can have it all.

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:27.990
I have some every day, so it's nothing special.

00:15:27.990 --> 00:15:31.610
Plus, I eat kind of funny.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:35.280
Did someone tell you that?

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:37.740
My parents.

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:40.870
I've never heard from anyone else, so...

00:15:40.870 --> 00:15:41.750
Anyone?

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:47.500
You've never eaten with anyone besides your parents?!

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:53.640
<i>Actually, now that I think about it, I was the same way up until now.</i>

00:15:54.550 --> 00:16:01.600
<i>It's because of the people around me that I was able to realize how good food is when it's eaten together.</i>

00:16:03.480 --> 00:16:05.110
<i>All right.</i>

00:16:05.650 --> 00:16:10.280
This is selfish of me, but I'm going to show you just how good it can be.

00:16:11.110 --> 00:16:13.780
Take a bite.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.910
You might experience something new.

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:18.660
B-B-But...

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:21.790
I've already tried all twenty varieties!

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.630
I haven't had anything but pizza for the past three weeks!

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.670
Your tummy's growling.

00:16:28.670 --> 00:16:30.460
Plus, this pizza's different!

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:34.550
Its flavor might be more... much more...

00:16:34.550 --> 00:16:38.060
It just might be more colorful than any of those twenty varieties!

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.020
C-Colorful?

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:45.560
<i>I'm not even sure what that means, but now I'm curious.</i>

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:48.570
O-Okay.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.230
Really?

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:52.320
A-All right...

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:54.660
Here goes.

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:09.750
It's incredible!

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.510
It's better than incredible!

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:19.100
The gratin pizza...

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:20.510
The squid...

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.930
The shrimp...

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:23.890
The white sauce...

00:17:24.270 --> 00:17:27.400
Then the sweetness of the corn ties it all together so nicely!

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:32.110
It's like a little girl dressed in white!

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:38.410
And then the barbecue's juicy meat
combined with the bite of the lemon

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.990
but with the texture of the sprouts giving it some depth...

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:44.450
It's like having a good, reliable friend.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:50.170
They all have their own flavors, and they're all so deep.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.260
So the pizza's like a friend to you.

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:02.350
That's wonderful, Uchiki!

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.560
W-Well...

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:09.690
Now I can't wait for my next slice.

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:14.820
There's only enough for two each, so choose carefully.

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.030
You know...

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:22.580
It's even tastier with a bit of spice.

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:25.330
That sounds great! Let me try it!

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:37.550
This is really good!

00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.010
Let me try it on my chicken too!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:43.220
Be careful. It's pretty spicy.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:46.770
It's hot, but it's great!

00:18:49.190 --> 00:18:51.560
<i>It looks like she's having fun.</i>

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:54.150
<i>I was worried that we might be intruding too much,</i>

00:18:54.150 --> 00:18:58.200
<i>but it looks like at least we didn't make her feel any worse about herself.</i>

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.410
These garlic-flavored potatoes...

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:10.000
That bit! It's like spring has sprung, right in my mouth!

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:13.750
You sound like Shiina saying that.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:16.710
Oh, Shiina's a friend of ours.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.260
Uchiki?

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:23.640
<i>I normally feel lonely after I eat,</i>

00:19:23.640 --> 00:19:26.430
<i>but today I can't stop smiling.</i>

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.100
Thanks again.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:35.270
Thank you too. That was wonderful.

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:39.740
You should come back sometime and try Ryo's cooking, Yuki.

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:42.280
I, uh, er...

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:45.240
Huh? That's your name, right?

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:47.870
Yes!

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:54.420
<i>That was lots of fun.</i>

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:59.010
<i>But even then, I didn't manage to say half of what I wanted to.</i>

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.340
<i>Still...</i>

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:05.800
<i>They gave me so much courage</i>

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:09.270
<i>and taught me a lot.</i>

00:20:10.600 --> 00:20:13.350
<i>Maybe I'm feeling up to this after all.</i>

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:18.440
Whoever would have expected we'd meet someone so nice so close by?

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:25.200
Yeah! I've learned that people truly shine when they're eating.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:32.120
I'm still worried, but I'm going to try hard to get into the school I want and keep up my appetite.

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:37.000
What do exams and your appetite have to do with each other?

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.760
Can you hang this one up too?

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:44.340
Sure.

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.260
Oh, hey, there's Yuki!

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:49.260
G-Good morning...

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:50.890
Good morning!

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:54.190
You look great in a suit.

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:59.780
I... I just have to go to a meeting.

00:20:59.780 --> 00:21:01.150
See you later.

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:03.780
Good luck!

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:07.570
She really is a grownup, huh?

00:21:07.570 --> 00:21:10.490
I thought she was closer to our age.

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.370
No way.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:18.710
Anyway, I hope she does well at her new job this spring.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.510
<i>Spring is still so far away.</i>

00:21:24.590 --> 00:21:25.930
<i>But...</i>

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:30.680
All right!

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:36.730
<i>Someday, spring will definitely come.</i>

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.440
See you next week!

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:43.070
See you next week.

00:21:57.920 --> 00:22:00.670
It's still cold, but...

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:46.400
Wait, Ryo, you just pour out the water you boiled the noodles in?!

00:23:46.400 --> 00:23:50.200
Doing it this way keeps it from
overwhelming the taste of the soup.

00:23:50.200 --> 00:23:54.530
What are you talking about? The oil from the noodles just makes it even smoother!

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:58.660
Why not just follow the instructions?

00:23:58.660 --> 00:24:00.750
That's what I'm saying!

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:05.000
Next time on Gourmet Girl Graffiti:

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:07.170
Crisp and Slippery!
